review_comments.body:
Not changed, on purpose. The proposed test relabels a message of `R20` with `R25`'s `numreponse` and serves it as page 4: that is a hand-built page state, which LESSONS 36 rules out. The real page `R25` redirects to (page 1100) has no captured body; the PR lists it under PENDING CAPTURE. Here is what the tests do cover without hand-building:
- the live source sends exactly `R25`'s request (`aMessageLinkAsksHFRForTheMessagesPageWithTheSession`);
- the page number comes from the final URL (existing `LiveTopicPageSourceTests` and `thePageServedWinsOverThePageAsked`);
- the model shows the served page at the message, scrolls without a fetch, and refreshes as a plain page request (`aMessageLinkOpensThePageHFRServesAtTheMessage`, with the scripted `FakeTopicPages`).

Once page 1100 is captured, a live-source test can check the anchor on the real page.

